WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.250 --> 00:00:07.642
Step 1: Under Drive Sync in the left sidebar, open Drives and click New or Sign in to connect a Google Drive account.

2
00:00:08.242 --> 00:00:15.922
Once authorized in your browser, Desk Console indexes free storage, file counts, and per-account proxy settings automatically.

3
00:00:16.522 --> 00:00:23.794
Step 2: Switch to Jobs and click New, then choose Two-way bisync mode with a 20-second Debounce settle time.

4
00:00:24.394 --> 00:00:30.658
Pick your PC folder and Google Drive folder right inside the dialog, complete with pre-filled junk exclude rules.

5
00:00:31.258 --> 00:00:39.394
Step 3: Use the top KPI strip to filter Synced, Syncing, or Failed jobs, and toggle real-time folder watchers.

6
00:00:39.994 --> 00:00:46.546
On the right rail, inspect every sync pass in History and read live rclone logs inside Console.

7
00:00:47.146 --> 00:00:53.266
Step 4: Click any job row to open its detail modal, adjust settings, or review the change log.

8
00:00:53.866 --> 00:01:00.490
The Folders tab merges your PC and Drive trees to compare files side by side and resolve conflicts in one click.

9
00:01:01.090 --> 00:01:09.994
Step 5: The Clips screen captures copied text, links, and images automatically, and lets you press Ctrl+Shift+Q to paste anywhere.

10
00:01:10.594 --> 00:01:16.738
Step 6: The Runners screen manages local services with one-click start/stop controls and a live console rail.

11
00:01:17.338 --> 00:01:24.394
Inside System, PC Optimizer monitors processes and reclaims background RAM in one click with Optimize All.

12
00:01:24.994 --> 00:01:32.938
Step 7: Fine-tune bandwidth limits and HTTP or SOCKS5 proxies with automatic Direct failover.

13
00:01:33.538 --> 00:01:40.066
Every deleted or overwritten file stays protected in Google Drive Trash and timestamped local backup folders.
